    "text": "1. Reliability: > Lack of reliability means losing a packet or ack, which entails retransmission. > For example, it is more important that electronic mail, file transfer, and Internet access have reliable transmissions than telephony or audio conferencing. 2. Delay: > “Applications can tolerate delay in different degrees. > Here, telephony, audio conferencing, video conferencing, and — need minimum delay, while delay in file transfer or e-mail is less important. 3. Jitter: > Variation in delay for packets belonging to the same flow. > if four packets depart at times 0, 1, 2, 3 and arrive at 20, 21, 22, 23, all have same delay of 20 units of time. But if these packets arrive at 21, 23, 21,28, they have different delays: 21,22, 19, and 24.",
